      "text": "To solve the system of equations, we can use the method of elimination. The given equations are:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3x - 5y & = -11,\\\\\n7x + 2y & = -12.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we will eliminate \\( y \\) by making the coefficients of \\( y \\) in both equations equal in magnitude but opposite in sign. To do this, we can multiply the first equation by 2 and the second equation by 5:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2(3x - 5y) & = 2(-11),\\\\\n5(7x + 2y) & = 5(-12).\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThis results in:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6x - 10y & = -22,\\\\\n35x + 10y & = -60.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNext, we add these two equations to eliminate \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n(6x - 10y) + (35x + 10y) &= -22 + (-60),\\\\\n6x + 35x &= -82,\\\\\n41x &= -82.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-82}{41} = -2.\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) back into the first original equation to solve for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3(-2) - 5y & = -11,\\\\\n-6 - 5y & = -11,\\\\\n-5y & = -11 + 6,\\\\\n-5y & = -5,\\\\\ny & = \\frac{-5}{-5},\\\\\ny & = 1.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(-2, 1)}\n\\]",
