      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the system of equations:\n\\[\n3x - 5y = -11,\n\\]\n\\[\n7x + 2y = -12,\n\\]\nwe can use the method of elimination or substitution. Here is the detailed step-by-step solution:\n\n1. **Multiply the equations by appropriate constants to eliminate one of the variables.**\n\nFirstly, let's eliminate \\( y \\) by making the coefficients of \\( y \\) in both equations equal. We can do this by finding the least common multiple (LCM) of the coefficients of \\( y \\) in both equations, which are 5 and 2. The LCM of 5 and 2 is 10.\n\nMultiply the first equation by 2:\n\\[\n2(3x - 5y) = 2(-11),\n\\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[\n6x - 10y = -22.\n\\]\n\nNow we have the system:\n\\[\n6x - 10y = -22,\n\\]\n\\[\n7x + 2y = -12.\n\\]\n\n2. **Add the two equations to eliminate \\( y \\).**\n\nAdding the above two equations:\n\\[\n(6x - 10y) + (7x + 2y) = -22 + (-12),\n\\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[\n13x - 8y = -34.\n\\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( x \\).**\n\nAt this point, we have:\n\\[\n13x - 8y = -34.\n\\]\n\nWe can isolate \\( x \\) by solving for \\( x \\):\n\\[\n13x = -34 + 8y,\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-34 + 8y}{13}.\n\\]\n\n4. **Substitute the expression for \\( x \\) back into one of the original equations to solve for \\( y \\).**\n\nLet's substitute \\( x \\) from the expression we just found back into the second original equation:\n\\[\n7\\left(\\frac{-34 + 8y}{13}\\right) + 2y = -12.\n\\]\n\nSimplify first:\n\\[\n\\frac{7(-34 + 8y)}{13} + 2y = -12,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{-238 + 56y}{13} + 2y = -12.\n\\]\n\nLet’s get rid of the fraction by multiplying the entire equation by 13:\n\\[\n-238 + 56y + 26y = -156,\n\\]\n\\[\n-238 + 82y = -156.\n\\]\n\nIsolate \\( y \\):\n\\[\n82y = -156 + 238,\n\\]\n\\[\n82y = 82,\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 1.\n\\]\n\n5. **Substitute the value of \\( y \\) back to find \\( x \\).**\n\nWe already have \\( y = 1 \\), and we can now substitute it back into one of the original equations to find \\( x \\). Using the first equation:\n\\[\n3x - 5(1) = -11,\n\\]\n\\[\n3x - 5 = -11,\n\\]\n\\[\n3x = -11 + 5,\n\\]\n\\[\n3x = -6,\n\\]\n\\[\nx = -2.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{( -2,1) }",
